  "sources": [
    {
      "file": "ddraw-colorkey-surface.c",
      "blobSha1": "b9300a98cf801690399d5f08f6977685123357b5",
      "sha256": "d24845b55037dac48f5dd5ce84cbed4d35cd0fc06e3ba419413dabdd484e8dd9",
      "url": "https://github.com/wine-mirror/wine/blob/415a275e3844c252ad385b46023095e9401ca234/dlls/ddraw/surface.c",
      "evidence": "Unlock, Blt and ReleaseDC route frontbuffer writes to ddraw_surface_update_frontbuffer. Actual coordinates and property tests are bridge implementation evidence, not a Microsoft HAL run."
    }
  ],
  "scope": "S2-50: one primary presentation helper used by Blt/BltFast/Unlock/ReleaseDC, including current flip-chain fronts. Windowed desktop-sized primary screen copies intersect surface/dirty bounds with the application client rectangle in screen coordinates, preferring the clipper HWND; no HWND preserves existing whole-primary fallback. Failed coordinate probes skip screen copies; signed 64-bit right/bottom avoid overflow. Accepted CPU/GDI/GPU update prefixes remain committed if screen resolve/Present fails. Native actual area/screen emitter/primary helper/Unlock/DC: 23658 checks, 10800 intersections, negative/offscreen/empty/window failures, overflow, window selection, primary versus offscreen, with/without chain and accepted-prefix errors. Thirteen strict-compiled runtime mutations; old actual screen emitter and write paths combined with current helper definitions strictly compile then fail clipping; not a complete previous-source bundle. XP actual five surface APIs, both windowed 800x600 desktop and 32x24 virtual fallback flip-chain fronts: forty immediate Blt/BltFast/WRITEONLY Unlock/GDI ReleaseDC frames without Flip. One initial GDI desktop seed, thirty deterministic CPU/GDI uploads, twenty native GPU blits, forty clipped screen copies, ten guest dirty-shadow readbacks. Zero-filled CPU readback replies are used only before complete overwrites; they do not validate GPU pixels. GPU replay validates 30720 actual resolved and 30720 displayed client pixels per backend plus exact desktop visibility masks. Five physical textures created; four explicit surface destruction commands, while the known implicit back-buffer CPU/storage cleanup leak remains S2-53. Both host devices retire all GPU resources through device cleanup; real driver owner releases once. No native HAL, genuine mode-switch acceptance, game/FPS, arbitrary clipper/occlusion/thread/device-loss/ownership completion, overlay Flip S2-51 or review stages 4/5/6 completion. Host/protocol/shader/bundle and D3D8/9 unchanged.",
  "facts": {
    "nativeChecks": 23658,
    "nativeIntersections": 10800,
    "newMutations": 13,
